            <section class="no-bg experience-detail-section">
              <span class="experience-section-kicker">02 · Case study</span>
              <h3 class="experience-section-title">DRIME Video Editor</h3>
              <h4>What it is</h4>
              <p>A standalone editor (distinct from the player) to create slideshows from short videos/photos with customizable transitions. Like the player, it’s multilingual, responsive, interactive, embeddable, and lightweight.</p>
              <h4>Speed of production</h4>
              <p>With pre-selected media and text, clients can create & publish a video in ~5 minutes. Adding another language (voiceover, subtitles, etc.) takes ~2 minutes. Logos and soundtracks can be added. In short, with minimal prep, a multilingual video can be produced in ~10 minutes and published immediately. Export via iframe, a single embed code line, or as a showcase on the DRIME platform.</p>
              <h4>Key Achievements — Editor</h4>
              <ul>
                <li>Set up the project on Heroku and installed it on GitHub.</li>
                <li>Created a third landing page with animations (scroll-unfolding video timeline, parallax, and other effects).</li>
                <li>Built the DRIME video editor from scratch (front end & back end).</li>
                <li>Implemented the app’s standard static pages.</li>
                <li>Created a Super Admin area to manage clients and their projects.</li>
                <li>Built a client area where clients can list, create, modify, duplicate, publish, and delete projects.</li>
                <li>Automated reading/writing of the required DRIME files on AWS for storage.</li>
                <li>Enabled user project creation, DRIME file creation, and video status management (temporary, draft, published).</li>
                <li>Added project options (editing choices, designs, responsive-mode focus).</li>
                <li>Enabled real-time previews of all effects upon selection.</li>
                <li>Integrated Azure Text-to-Speech (voiceovers) with gender/region filters; users can sample each selected voice on a personalized DRIME sample translated into all languages; supported custom pronunciations and deletion/editing.</li>
                <li>Integrated Azure Translator for project translations, with manual client overrides.</li>
                <li>Enabled project preview before publishing and draft saving.</li>
                <li>Migrated the project to GitLab, Docker, and AWS, in collaboration with an independent architect who built the new environment.</li>
              </ul>
